WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.912
Chapter 02 states the problem precisely.

2
00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:07.575
Active Directory shipped with Windows
2000 as an identity directory.

3
00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:12.056
Over twenty-five years every Windows-era
service wired itself into it,

4
00:00:12.056 --> 00:00:17.387
because it was the only enterprise-wide,
governed, replicated namespace available.

5
00:00:17.387 --> 00:00:19.925
Nobody wrote down how much
governance it carried.

6
00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:24.200
The organizational unit (OU)
tree wasn't a folder system.

7
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.478
Placing one user in a branch handed
the account to that branch's delegated

8
00:00:28.478 --> 00:00:32.335
administrators, applied every
Group Policy linked along the path,

9
00:00:32.335 --> 00:00:35.000
fed the tools that built
groups from position,

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.138
bound the account to the branch's
delegation, and drew an audit boundary.

11
00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.025
One act, five effects.

12
00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:46.437
Entra ID has no OU tree, so each
effect has to be rebuilt on purpose.

13
00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:51.425
Most migration plans count users,
computers, groups and Group Policy.

14
00:00:51.425 --> 00:00:54.982
The program's inventory
counts eleven categories,

15
00:00:54.982 --> 00:00:59.641
adding service accounts and service
principal names, DNS and DHCP,

16
00:00:59.641 --> 00:01:05.400
certificate services, RADIUS, LDAP-bound
applications and trust relationships.

17
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.751
Those fail silently: a
certificate that doesn't renew,

18
00:01:08.751 --> 00:01:12.712
an application whose bind account
was deleted with the domain.

19
00:01:12.712 --> 00:01:15.188
No log line says governance has failed.

20
00:01:15.188 --> 00:01:18.126
Microsoft hasn't deprecated
Active Directory.

21
00:01:18.126 --> 00:01:20.169
It still supports and enhances it,

22
00:01:20.169 --> 00:01:24.475
while pointing customers toward a
cloud-first model reached in phases.

23
00:01:24.475 --> 00:01:28.813
So there's no vendor deadline;
retiring it is the agency's decision.

24
00:01:28.813 --> 00:01:32.289
That makes scope a decision
for the sponsor and the CIO:

25
00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:36.924
fund this as a governance transformation
across all eleven categories,

26
00:01:36.924 --> 00:01:40.850
not a users-and-groups project,
when scope and funding are set.
